From b0fddc84e59ac6293b88396963a3cde99c2189b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mrinohk <5554998+Mrinohk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 11:29:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 20/31] cuda : MTP verify output layer and flash attention
 kernels for sm_60

Two more pieces of the 2..6 token verify pass under GGML_CUDA_P60_MEGA=1:

- Dense q8_0 MUL_MAT with K = 2048 and 2..6 columns (p60-mega-t.cu, called from mmvq-p60): persistent grid, x in
  shared memory as power-of-2-scaled fp16 like the single-column path, rows streamed in 1088 B chunks. Output layer
  (248k rows) at 6 columns: 2829 -> 1686 us. GGML_CUDA_P60_Q8T=0 disables it.
- Flash attention for 2..6 tokens, head size 256, GQA 8, f16 K/V (p60-fa.cu, called from fattn.cu): one block per KV
  head and position range holds all T x 8 query rows, so K/V are read once (the tile kernel uses 4-token column
  blocks and converts every fp16 product to fp32 at quarter rate). HFMA2 chains of 32 products flushed to fp32, fp32
  softmax and accumulators, a second kernel merges the ranges. 6 tokens at 28k context: 710 -> 382 us, at 4k:
  140 -> 79 us. GGML_CUDA_P60_FA=0 disables it.

2x P100, Qwen3.6-35B-A3B UD-Q4_K_XL, MTP n5 + draft vocab, prod sampler:
  8 prompts x 256 tokens: 151.2 -> 160.8 t/s
  28k-token prompt:        ~123 -> ~141 t/s
test-backend-ops matches the CPU backend for both. Wikitext KLD vs the stock ub=1 base at -ub 6: 0.00420 (previous
mega path 0.00430, stock 0.00390), same top token 97.55% (stock 97.53%).

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
